    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25cd606c_1f6cbea5",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/chip/npcx/ram_lock.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 3306924
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-26T07:44:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the input parameter is fixed, we have simplified the computation by directly using LOG2(NPCX_RAM_BLOCK) as the natural_alignment. This eliminates the need for additional alignment calculations ([implementation](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/npcx/ram_lock.c;drc\u003da8b8b850ccc36b704f823094b62339662f6a7077;l\u003d74)). Similarly, the NPCX_RAM_SECTOR is directly used as the subregion_size value in the later computation. Do you recommend keeping the implementation consistent on both sides?",
      "parentUuid": "9ae3927a_9e8162d4",
      "revId": "4a40f877b360fcbe206ca1d8d7921f5f543cf713",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
